          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मोकळा (mokḷā) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from mukna, \"loosed\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants (CDIAL 10157). CDIAL compares mukta, \"loosed\", and suggests the -o- may come from mokṣa, \"release\". It glosses the Marathi word \"free\"."
